# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Node (only relevant if/when OpenSpec runs locally)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Python (tools/*.py helper scripts, e.g. pre_merge_check.py, check_version_docs.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local secrets / runtime config
.env
.env.local
*.local.json

# Certificates and private keys — must never enter version control
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.crt

# ASP.NET local-environment overrides — may contain real credentials
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json

# Ad-hoc secrets files
secrets.json

# .NET build outputs
/obj/
/bin/
src/**/obj/
src/**/bin/
tools/**/obj/
tools/**/bin/
tests/**/obj/
tests/**/bin/
qa/**/obj/
qa/**/bin/
*.user

# Test results and coverage
TestResults/
coverage*/
*.coverage

# CI artefact files — generated locally; do not commit (CI uploads them as artefacts)
traceability.md
traceability-local.md
licence-inventory.md

# Working / scratch notes (not part of the repo)
resume.txt
notes/

# Ad-hoc Playwright/Node scaffolding for browser-driven UAT scripts (e.g. D-LINUX-001
# DOM-inspection verification). Reinstallable on demand; never a deliverable.
qa/uat-tmp/

# D001 PCM-SIC development corpus — real off-air WAVs and ALL.TXT logs containing
# real third-party callsigns; local only (NFR-021 / GDPR).
D001-pcm-sic_items/

# Daemon runtime output — generated files
ALL.TXT

# ADIF QSO logs — contain real third-party callsigns (NFR-021 / GDPR); local only
ADIF.log
*.adif

# Cycle audio archive (cycle-audio-archive capability) — real off-air audio and real
# third-party callsigns (NFR-021). The default archive directory is the platform per-user
# app-data directory, outside the repo; these entries are defence in depth in case an
# operator points the "directory" setting at (or under) the repo itself.
cycle-audio/
cycle-archive.csv

# Operator / debug tools — binaries placed at repo root during investigations
procdump*.exe
procdump*.zip

# Local tool output — generated by running CI tools locally; CI uploads these as artefacts
traceability-check-local.md

# Live on-air run artefacts — may contain real third-party callsigns (NFR-021 / GDPR);
# local only, never commit.
artefacts/

# Native build artifacts — obj files and intermediate DLL.
# r0-reproducible-native-build: message.obj's carve-out (it had been binary-patched, D-006,
# shim 20260015, with no source-level fix ever written) is REMOVED here. message.c now compiles
# from native/ft8_lib_vendor/ on every rebuild_shim.bat invocation (with the D-006 fix restored
# at the source level via a build-side-only compat header, see stpcpy_msvc_compat.h) — tracking
# a pre-built copy of an object every clean build regenerates from source has no purpose. All obj
# files, including message.obj, are now untracked build intermediates.
native/ft8_lib_build/obj/*
native/ft8_lib_build/linux_obj/
native/ft8_lib_build/*.obj
native/ft8_lib_build/*.exp
native/ft8_lib_build/*.lib
native/ft8_lib_build/libft8.dll
native/ft8_lib_build/libft8.so

# Scratch comparison binaries placed at repo root (not the committed platform binaries)
baseline_libft8.dll

# Serena MCP tool — logs and runtime artefacts (project config is committed)
daemon_log.txt

# Application log files (FR-022) — operator artefacts, not source
logs/

# Claude Code runtime lock file — local only, not source
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# S6 corpus replay — raw ALL.TXT snapshots contain real third-party callsigns (NFR-021).
# Committed artifacts (report.md, summary.csv, *.png) are scrubbed by analyse_corpus.py.
qa/rr-study/results/corpus-*/raw/
qa/rr-study/results/corpus-*/run_manifest.json

# S6 corpus replay — raw console transcript of the replay step itself (WAV filenames +
# timestamps only, no callsigns, so no NFR-021 risk). Pure scratch, fully superseded by the
# committed report.md once analyse_corpus.py has run — never worth tracking.
qa/rr-study/results/*/replay_run.log

# D-009 / OSD false-positive evidence — S5 AWGN decode files ALWAYS contain OSD CRC-14
# coincidences (ITU-assignable callsign patterns) → NFR-021 violation if committed.
# S7 high-scene-complexity files carry the same risk (noise-floor FPs at −27 dB).
# Both must remain local only and must be reviewed / scrubbed before any commit.
owsfz-s5-all.txt
owsfz-s7-all.txt
openswfz-*.log

# Same rule, different naming convention: the ablation-study harness (run_ablation.py)
# writes the plain filename "owsfz-all.txt" inside a directory suffixed "-s5" instead of
# encoding "s5" into the filename itself (e.g. cfg1-s5/owsfz-all.txt). Same NFR-021 risk,
# same "never commit" rule — this pattern just matches the directory-name convention.
**/*-s5/owsfz-all.txt

# Same rule, third naming convention: ad-hoc dated re-check run directories under
# qa/rr-study/results/ (e.g. d011-fp-recheck-2026-07-04/, produced by run_scenario.py)
# hold the same raw appraiser decode logs and matched CSV — same NFR-021 risk, never
# commit. Scoped to filename so the accompanying report.md/report.html/*.png stay tracked.
qa/rr-study/results/*/owsfz-all.txt
qa/rr-study/results/*/wsjt-all.txt
qa/rr-study/results/*/*_matched.csv

# Fourth naming convention, found 2026-08-22: a harness wrote a SUFFIXED copy
# ("owsfz-all.txt.livecopy-preclear") of an ignored file. The exact-filename rules above
# matched the original and walked straight past the copy, leaving real off-air callsigns
# untracked-but-committable in a public repo. Same NFR-021 risk; same never-commit rule.
# Prefix-matched so no future suffix can reopen the same hole (cf. qa-backlog N14 --
# harnesses choosing output filenames the repo's guards do not anticipate).
qa/rr-study/results/*/owsfz-all.txt.*
qa/rr-study/results/*/wsjt-all.txt.*

# P-LIVE per-row BER dumps — tens of MB per stage, regenerable from the harness
# plus the corpus. The committed *_report.json carries every gated statistic.
# Retained copies live under artefacts/ (blanket-ignored above).
# Ruling: qa/rr-study/2026-08-18-1616-architect-to-qa-p-live-stage1-ruling-anchor-provenance-defect.md Sec.5.3.1
qa/rr-study/p-live-population/results/*_rows.json

# Linux cross-platform R&R — runtime artefacts generated at repo root during WSL2 sessions.
# These are operator files, not source, and may contain callsigns (NFR-021).
linux-all.txt

# Same rule, Windows side of the same xplat pilot (found 2026-08-23 NFR-021 151-file audit —
# qa/rr-study/results/2026-07-01-b03998f/windows-all.txt was tracked and contaminated).
windows-all.txt

# r2-coherent-llr-instrument AC-N1 replay corpora — full decode replays of the real
# WINDOW_20M 20m off-air window (b_dt_c1/c3 sibling arms' report.json/run.log carry no
# "message" field and are unaffected). Confirmed by QA 2026-08-22 (fix-negative-time-
# offset-snr-collapse review): every replay_*.json file's "message" values are real,
# assignable-format amateur callsigns (e.g. SJ6AVS, VA7ZM, KB7AWG) — NFR-021 violation,
# merge-blocking, regardless of how the change proposal that produces them describes
# them ("committed"). Never commit; regenerate locally via the harness against the
# pinned DLL when a regression check needs to be re-run.
qa/rr-study/r2-coherent-llr-instrument/results/replay_*.json
linux-daemon.log

# Native build diagnostic variants — intermediate DLLs produced during
# D-009 / libft8_cfg* ablation builds; not source-controlled.
native/ft8_lib_build/libft8_cfg*.dll
native/ft8_lib_build/libft8_diag*.dll
native/ft8_lib_build/libft8_prod_backup.dll
native/ft8_lib_build/rebuild_*.txt
